# MongoDB is deliberately NOT installed on the host any more.
#
# Every MongoDB build from 4.4.19 onwards requires ARMv8.2-A atomics (LSE).
# The gateway's Cortex-A72 is ARMv8.0-A -- "lscpu" lists no "atomics" flag --
# so mongod 6.0.30 was killed with SIGILL on the first boot that got far
# enough to run it. 4.4.18 is the last version this CPU executes, and it links
# libssl1.1, which trixie does not ship: there is no version that satisfies
# both constraints natively.
#
# It therefore runs as a container (service "wazigate-mongo" in
# /var/lib/wazigate/docker-compose.yml, from the WaziGate repo), which carries
# its own OpenSSL 1.1 while the host stays on OpenSSL 3. The container uses
# network_mode: host and binds 127.0.0.1:27017, exactly where /usr/bin/wazigate
# expects it, so nothing else changed.
